From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 11:17:33 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(onboarding): graceful Windows setup + one-step setup/init

FIX 1 (048c1e6d): ensureWorkflowShellPolicy no longer hard-throws when Git
Bash is absent on Windows. It now prints install guidance (git-scm.com) and
returns a degraded policy so core setup finishes in reduced-capability mode;
behavior is unchanged when Git Bash is present.

FIX 2 (ac0b38c7): setup now runs `forge init` (standard profile,
non-interactive) at completion when .forge/config.yaml is absent, via a new
finalizeWorkflowConfig helper that reuses init's real handler. Falls back to
the printed guidance on failure. `forge init` still works standalone.

Also: QUICKSTART clarifies slash-skills (/plan,/dev,/validate,/ship,/review,
/verify) vs typeable `forge` CLI verbs, and documents one-step setup +
Windows degrade. Adds tests for both paths.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
